                {
                  "phase": "grammar",
                  "type": "grammar_rule",
                  "content": {
                    "title": "Past perfect and narrative tenses",
                    "explanation": "El past perfect (had + participio) cuenta algo que pasó antes de otro momento del pasado: When we arrived, the band had already started (primero empezó el grupo, luego llegamos).\n\nPara contar historias combinamos tres tiempos:\n• past simple para los hechos principales: We arrived late.\n• past continuous para la situación de fondo: Everyone was singing.\n• past perfect para lo que pasó antes: Daniel had left the tickets at home.\n\nPalabras frecuentes: already, never… before, by the time, because.",
                    "table": {
                      "headers": [
                        "Tiempo",
                        "Uso",
                        "Ejemplo"
                      ],
                      "rows": [
                        [
                          "Past simple",
                          "hechos principales",
                          "We arrived at nine."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Past continuous",
                          "situación de fondo",
                          "Everyone was singing."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Past perfect",
                          "algo anterior",
                          "The band had already started."
                        ],
                        [
                          "Pregunta",
                          "Had + sujeto + participio",
                          "Had they started?"
                        ],
                        [
                          "Negativa",
                          "hadn't",
                          "He hadn't played there before."
                        ]
                      ]
                    },
                    "examples": [
                      "When we arrived, the band had already started.",
                      "Daniel had left the tickets at home, so we had to go back.",
                      "He had never played in front of so many people.",
                      "Luckily, Sam had brought his old guitar."
                    ]
                  }
                },
